=======================================================================
             The Optical Gravitational Lensing Experiment.
                The OGLE-III Catalog of Variable Stars.
           IX. RR Lyrae Stars in the Small Magellanic Cloud

   I. Soszynski, A. Udalski, M.K. Szymanski, M. Kubiak, G. Pietrzynski,
              L. Wyrzykowski, K. Ulaczyk, and R. Poleski

=======================================================================
soszynsk@astrouw.edu.pl


This directory contains the ninth part of the OGLE-III Catalog of Variable
Stars - RR Lyrae stars in the Small Magellanic Cloud.

The directory structure is as follows:

README            - this file

ident.dat         - identification of stars

RRab.dat          - parameters of RRab stars
RRc.dat           - parameters of RRc stars
RRd.dat           - parameters of RRd stars
RRe.dat           - parameters of RRe stars

phot/I/           - I-band photometry of individual objects
phot/V/           - V-band photometry of individual objects
phot.tar.gz       - gzipped phot/ directory

fcharts/          - finding charts of individual objects
                       
remarks.txt       - remarks on selected objects

pap.ps.gz         - postscript version of the paper Soszynski et al. (2010),
                    Acta Astron. 60, 165, (arXiv:1009.0528) describing the
                    catalog.


Format of the file ident.dat:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes  Format Units   Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 19  A19   ---     Star's ID in the form OGLE-SMC-RRLYR-NNNN
 22- 29  A8    ---     OGLE-III field
 31- 36  I6    ---     OGLE-III database number
 38- 41  A5    ---     Subtype of RR Lyr star (RRab, RRc, RRd, RRe)
 44- 45  I2    h       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (hours)
 47- 48  I2    m       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (minutes)
 50- 54  F5.2  s       Right ascension, equinox J2000.0 (seconds)
     56  A1    ---     Declination, equinox J2000.0 (sign)
 57- 58  I2    deg     Declination, equinox J2000.0 (degrees)
 60- 61  I2    arcmin  Declination, equinox J2000.0 (arc minutes)
 63- 66  F4.1  arcsec  Declination, equinox J2000.0 (arc seconds)
 68- 82  A15   ---     OGLE-II ID
 84- 88  A5    ---     GCVS ID
 90-     A     ---     Other designation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Format of the files RRab.dat, RRc.dat, and RRe.dat:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes  Format Units   Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 19  A19   ---     Star's ID in the form OGLE-SMC-RRLYR-NNNNN
 22- 27  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean I-band magnitude
 29- 34  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean V-band magnitude
 36- 45  F10.7 days    Period
 47- 55  F9.7  days    Uncertainty of period
 58- 67  F10.5 days    Time of maximum brightness (HJD-2450000)
 70- 74  F5.3  mag     I-band amplitude (maximum-minimum)
 77- 81  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_21
 83- 87  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_21
 90- 94  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_31
 96-100  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_31
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Format of the file RRd.dat:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes  Format Units   Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1- 19  A19   ---     Star's ID in the form OGLE-SMC-RRLYR-NNNNN
 22- 27  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean I-band magnitude
 29- 34  F6.3  mag     Intensity mean V-band magnitude
 36- 45  F10.7 days    First-overtone period
 47- 55  F9.7  days    Uncertainty of first-overtone period
 58- 67  F10.5 days    Time of maximum brightness (HJD-2450000)
 70- 74  F5.3  mag     I-band amplitude (maximum-minimum)
 77- 81  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_21
 83- 87  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_21
 90- 94  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_31
 96-100  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_31
102-111  F10.7 days    Fundamental-mode period
113-121  F9.7  days    Uncertainty of Fundamental-mode period
124-133  F10.5 days    Time of maximum brightness (HJD-2450000)
136-140  F5.3  mag     I-band amplitude (maximum-minimum)
143-147  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_21
149-153  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_21
156-160  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient R_31
162-166  F5.3  ---     Fourier coefficient phi_31
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Finding charts are gzipped Postscript images. The names of the files are in
the form: OGLE-SMC-RRLYR-NNNN.ps.gz. The finding charts are 60"x60" subframes
of the I-band reference frames centered on the star. White cross marks the
star. North is up and East to the left.


Any presentation of the scientific analysis or usage of the data from the
catalog of RR Lyrae stars in the SMC should include the appropriate
reference(s) to OGLE paper(s).
